WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Auto-Attendant] All
of our representatives

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:04.861
are currently busy.
Please stay on the line

00:00:04.861 --> 00:00:05.900
and your call will be answered

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.073
by the next available representative.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.350
Today's customer hates
to wait for service.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.930
When I call up a brand
or a service provider,

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.510
I expect to get my
questions answered quickly

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.833
and to my satisfaction.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.080
In the world of customer service,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.970
the challenge is to stay a step ahead

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.650
of customer expectations

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.660
and ensure that every brand interaction

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.059
is not just positive, but
delightful for the customer.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.330
My name is Manish Goyal

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.700
and I'm a Senior Partner
in IBM Consulting,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.340
leading our AI analytics
business globally.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.410
The goal of my team is to help our clients

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.770
apply AI analytics and
automation to create insights

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.870
that drive better decisions.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.960
And one of the areas I
spend a lot of time in

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.910
is advising clients on how
AI analytics can help deliver

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.640
delightful customer experiences.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.070
This could be through
self-service experiences

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.200
or through aiding human agents

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.840
with tools and insights
so that they can deliver

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.673
a great experience to the customer.

00:01:21.694 --> 00:01:24.090
Now, enterprises spend billions of dollars

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.833
on customer service every year.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:27.840
Good customer service

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.070
can turn one-time clients into
long-term brand champions.

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.380
And the lifetime value of an NPS promoter

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.460
can be 10 times more
than an NPS detractor.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.700
On the other hand, around
80% of consumers say

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.890
they would rather do
business with a competitor

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:46.860
after more than one bad
experience with a brand.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.940
The contact center,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.460
the hub of most customer
service operations,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.580
has come a long way in the
past couple of decades.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.060
Tools such as interactive
voice response (IVR),

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:00.630
agent assist, robotic process
automation and chat bots

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.560
have already made customer
service agents more productive.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.790
However, at most enterprises,
the use of these technologies

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.610
is fragmented instead of seamless.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.870
At the same time,

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.470
customer expectations continue
to be more and more demanding

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:20.010
these days, especially
coming out of the pandemic.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.550
Customers expect seamless
access and speedy resolution

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:27.090
to their queries across
digital and voice channels.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.000
This in turn puts pressure on businesses

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.257
to deliver a frictionless
customer experience

00:02:32.257 --> 00:02:36.150
at every stage, from
discovery to purchase,

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.430
through service and retention.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.570
Now with generative AI,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.360
this experience can be
taken to the next level.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.720
Large language models have the
power to significantly expand

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.220
what can be automated,

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.350
performing critical customer service tasks

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:53.460
that are far beyond the capacities
of earlier technologies.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.310
These models are trained
on vast amounts of data

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.130
and can recognize, classify, and create

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:02.973
sophisticated text and speech
with speed and precision.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:04.980
To see how

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.310
generative AI can significantly
improve customer service,

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.560
let's look at three key areas.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.060
The first is self-service,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:16.410
wherein you give the tools to
customers to serve themselves.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.950
Virtual agents or chatbots
serve the purpose here.

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:22.140
And over the years, they
have become very good

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.360
at being able to direct customers

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:26.970
down a predetermined journey.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.230
To make these journeys,

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.650
you first analyze what
people are asking about,

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:32.940
you understand their intent

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.950
and then handcraft the dialogue flows

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.413
to direct them down the right journeys.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.910
In the past, creating
these flows took time,

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.440
but now with generative AI,

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:46.773
you can deliver much richer
self-service experiences.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.400
These experiences are more
natural and conversational.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.850
They're more resilient to
variations and digressions,

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.550
and the tooling to create these flows

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.700
is also now being augmented
with generative AI,

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.400
so that the process area
and domain area experts

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:05.700
can describe the journeys
in natural language

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:09.480
and AI generates the
necessary underlying flows.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.350
The second area,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.450
where generative AI can
significantly improve

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.990
customer experience is by
augmenting the human agent,

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:19.200
whether in the contact
center or in the field.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.350
A lot of time is spent by
agents in the contact center

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.030
searching knowledge bases

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.520
to resolve the queries for customers.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.940
Generative AI can dramatically
improve the retrieval

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:32.130
of this information
from the knowledge bases

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.400
and present it back to
agents in a summarized way,

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.520
to help resolve the
customer query quickly.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.680
This cuts down the time that
the customer is on hold,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.120
improving their experience,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.910
while also allowing the
agent to handle more calls

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.530
during their shift.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:49.200
Similarly, field service
agents can be armed

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.060
with generative AI based solutions

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.370
that help them troubleshoot
problems in the field

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.293
faster and more accurately.

00:04:56.637 --> 00:04:58.290
Another good example

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:02.130
is helping agents draft email
responses automatically,

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.530
based on the context or query,

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.240
allowing them to review and edit

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.100
before responding to the customer.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.450
AI augmented emails

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.620
have shown to have a higher
satisfaction score by customers.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.980
And the third area is in
contact center operations.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.320
Let's say you have a
call center of a thousand

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:21.480
or maybe ten thousand agents.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.670
Gaining insights into what's happening

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.170
across all the conversations

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.600
taking place between agents and customers

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.180
was difficult or expensive before.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.910
With generative AI, you can
go through the transcripts

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:36.600
of every call made and
continuously gather insights

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.720
on how and why agents
are taking a long time

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.430
to handle certain types of calls,

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:44.910
or understanding granular
classification of complaints

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.233
on products or services.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.220
This insight that a application
of generative AI provides

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:53.850
can allow your operations
leaders to find the root cause

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.280
of a problem faster and resolve them,

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.840
if in the servicing function,

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.360
or alert the product or marketing teams,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.640
if they need to take remedial action.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.740
There's also a lot of time spent by agents,

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.480
after each call with a customer,

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.850
documenting a summary
of their conversations

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:09.873
and actions taken.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.900
During that after call work time,

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.840
they're unavailable to attend a new call.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.610
Again, with generative AI,

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.290
you can transcribe in real time

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.180
the conversation that they're having

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.430
and generate a draft of the summary

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:27.540
that agents can then edit and
feed back into the CRM system.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.400
Not only does this drive consistency

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.730
in capturing details of each
conversation with customers,

00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.280
but it also saves time
and drives productivity

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.333
for the agents.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.880
Today, as the cost of building
these solution comes down

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.570
with foundation models and
the ROI becomes justifiable,

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.100
there's a renewed focus

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:54.000
on the ways generative AI can
be used for customer service.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.340
And it's not difficult to imagine why!

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.860
Customer service has always been complex.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.870
Just think of the last time you called in

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.400
for customer service.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.820
Chances are you wanted to
address a problem you were facing

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:09.060
with a purchase or a product
or a service you have;

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:12.150
and if you have a problem,
you are generally unhappy,

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:15.870
which is why enabling service
journeys that anticipate

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.410
and deliver delightful
omnichannel experiences,

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.120
whether as a self-service function

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:24.210
or a human assisted one is critical.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.420
Secondly, in some companies,
there are a lot of employees

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.223
who can influence the
experience customers have

00:07:29.223 --> 00:07:31.380
with the brand or service.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.030
If you can augment their skills

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.180
and drive productivity
across this large population

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.800
who front your brand,

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.350
it'll be a huge win for your enterprise.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.390
And given the capabilities of AI

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:44.670
and the rate at which it is evolving,

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:47.416
you can expect significant
gains in productivity

00:07:47.416 --> 00:07:49.590
with the right deployment.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:51.030
And there's more!

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:54.330
As businesses focus on building
omnichannel experiences

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.830
for their customers,

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.710
AI can power interactions
or conversations

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:01.530
irrespective of the channel
customers come in from.

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:02.970
Which means a customer request

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.220
that originated in one channel

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.253
can be completed in another
channel, seamlessly.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.620
Combining traditional
AI with generative AI

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.260
enterprises can drive proactive outreach,

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.743
helping avoid problems or
help resolve them faster.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.450
If you were to look closely
at how these companies achieve

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.390
high levels of coordination
amongst their channels,

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:34.200
you will discover a five step
approach driving the execution.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.770
The first step, as you kick
off, is to have a clear idea

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:40.590
of the experience you want to deliver.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.470
Next is to understand your customers well.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:47.670
What is the demographic,
preferences, digital or voice?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:51.390
And now that you know your
audience, you need to determine

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.800
how you want to serve them,

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.680
decide what channels you
want to direct them to.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.270
And then, look at the best tools

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.250
that can support those channels.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.630
So what is your platform?

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:03.990
Do you go with the cloud-based
contact center solution?

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:08.010
Will it be on-premises for
other reasons, or something else?

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.050
Once you have your tool chain sorted,

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:13.440
the final step is to design
the journey end-to-end,

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:15.390
so it delivers on the service strategy,

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:18.510
the experience you had
defined when you started.

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:21.360
My favorite story, and
it really warms my heart

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.010
whenever I speak of this,

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:24.360
is the work that we have been doing

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:27.390
with the US Veterans Affairs since 2019.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:30.180
Before we came in, it used
to take a really long time

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.550
for veterans to get their benefits.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:34.650
We applied analytics and automation

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:37.650
to help support faster claim creation

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:39.213
and response to veterans.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:44.190
Just a few numbers: 3 million
packets processed end-to-end,

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:47.940
and these packets have
lots of documents in them.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.400
280 different document types,

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.240
24 distinct mail type processes,

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.810
100% automation of all mail intake.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:01.563
We are processing 220,000
documents per week.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.250
We then took that process further,

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.270
by applying sophisticated AI
to analyze the medical records.

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:11.610
We are now helping the claims adjudicator

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.860
make decisions faster,

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:16.456
so that the veterans who
fought for our country

00:10:16.456 --> 00:10:19.800
get the help they need
without the long wait.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:24.800
And since 2023, we have
processed over 125,000 claims.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.490
We have been expecting AI
to make a big difference

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:30.897
for quite some time now.

00:10:30.897 --> 00:10:32.490
And I think the capabilities

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.770
have finally caught up with the hype.

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:38.640
What's more, the innovation
rate has also accelerated

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.613
dramatically, with a new
announcement almost every week.

00:10:42.613 --> 00:10:45.330
It is becoming increasingly evident now

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.490
that the faster you add the capabilities

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:49.830
of generative AI to your organization,

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.250
the sooner you can make use
of the unlimited opportunities

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.840
it opens up.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.660
Imagine the next time your
customer runs into a problem

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.660
and needs help: You'll
have all the capabilities

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.930
to turn a possibly adverse situation

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:07.410
into a positive experience,
without making them wait,

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:10.710
and perhaps, even before
they pick up the phone.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:11.543
So the question for enterprises

00:11:11.543 --> 00:11:14.400
looking to fold AI into
their customer service

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.089
is no longer, "Why?" But "When?"

